# Lockfile and graph safety

- Treat package metadata records separately from resolved package instances.
- Preserve peer-context identities.
- Preserve distinct package instances that differ by peer providers, patch identity, protocol, or other semantic context.
- Do not invent phantom installed package instances from metadata-only records.
- Resolve dependency references against the actual canonical target set.
- Preserve alias labels separately from actual target package identities.
- Preserve workspace references separately from registry packages.
- Preserve patched and unpatched instances distinctly.
- Return typed errors for: empty references; malformed references; dangling references; ambiguous references; unsupported protocols; invalid identities; conflicting producer evidence.
- Never use a guessed fallback after resolution failure.
- Never silently omit an edge when encoding fails.
- Propagate encoding failures through the full write and transaction chain.
- Preserve original incumbent bytes after any failed mutation.
